 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spc-001"></a>
+
+The clinic publishes its specialties, each shown by its stored name together with the veterinarians who hold it, listed by full name — first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary" `[REQ-SPC-001]`. The page lists specialties, not the full veterinarian roster: a veterinarian holding no specialty appears under no specialty and so does not appear on this page. Every specialty appears together on one page, with no paging. The page is reachable by its own address alone; no navigation entry and no link from another page carries the reader to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened at its address, then every specialty is listed by its stored name, each with the veterinarians who hold it shown by full name — first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian does not appear on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging control.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the directory, when the surface is surveyed, then it is reachable only by its own address, with no navigation entry and no link from another page pointing to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. Managing veterinarians or their specialties stays out of scope — the page only reads and presents the stored collection (NG-2).
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each specialty, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one. Which stable order is an open question — see [Open Questions](#open-questions).
+3. A specialty held by no veterinarian is still listed, shown as held by none — the page lists every specialty the clinic knows. Whether this reading is intended is an open question — see [Open Questions](#open-questions).
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
